  "body": "**Pocket recognition reads an inside-out mesh as a pocket the size of the part.** This is on main since #512 merged (head 7e39726). The maintainer's review found it before the merge.\n\n`recognize::pockets_of` (`crates/app/src/recognize/mod.rs`) takes \"up\" and \"leans into\" straight from the facet winding. It never asks the body-winding verdict that #387 added (`pick/winding.rs`, `verdict_for` / `refusal`, used by `pick/align.rs`).\n\n**What happens:** a plain 10 mm cube with every facet reversed returns `Ok([Pocket { kind: Closed, floor_z: 0.0, .. }])`. Its bottom face now \"faces up\" and its outer walls \"lean in\", so the part's own outline is reported as a closed pocket as deep as the part. A reversed pocketed block is reported the same way. `detect_pockets` with `create` would then make a Pocket over the part's footprint, cut down to its base: a gouge through the whole part.\n\n**Done means:**\n- `pockets_of` runs the winding verdict first and returns its refusal by name, as the pick tools do. A torn or open mesh takes the same route.\n- The refusal is pinned by tests with a reversed cube, a reversed pocket block and a torn mesh.\n",
